# Front LAUNCH-3 [W]: language addresses people type that are not the site's own, sent with a 301 to the page that exists
# (docs/DEPLOY.md § 12). Cloudflare Pages applies this file from the output directory before any asset; it is not served.
# Pages keeps the request's query string when the destination has none. src/seo/redirects.test.ts checks every line against
# the language table (src/seo/languages.ts); tests/release/pages-smoke.pages.ts checks the answers under `wrangler pages dev`.
# A redirect wins over an asset at the same path, so no rule may name a path the build emits.
#
# Portuguese: /pt and /pt/… go to the Brazilian Portuguese pages under /pt-br/, keeping the rest of the path. No rule for
# /pt-BR: a source that differs from /pt-br/ only in case would loop if a host ever matched paths without regard to case.
/pt /pt-br/ 301
/pt/* /pt-br/:splat 301
# English lives at the root: /en and /en/… drop the prefix.
/en / 301
/en/* /:splat 301
# Spanish: the UI tag es-419 (as in ?lang=es-419) goes to the Spanish pages under /es/.
/es-419 /es/ 301
/es-419/* /es/:splat 301
